.TH "PACKETD" "8" "October 26, 2026" "ka9q-radio" "ka9q-radio Manual"
.SH NAME
packetd \- decode 1200-baud AFSK AX.25 from receiver audio
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B packetd
.RI "[options] [-I input ...] -R output [input ...]"
.SH DESCRIPTION
packetd receives demodulated PCM audio, decodes 1200-baud AFSK AX.25 frames,
and sends decoded frames in RTP to an output group. Multiple audio groups may
be monitored. It is a software packet demodulator, not an APRS-IS gateway;
aprsfeed provides the latter function.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B "\-I destination, \-\-pcm\-in destination"
Add a PCM input group. May be repeated; positional groups are also accepted.
.TP
.B "\-R destination, \-\-ax25\-out destination"
Set decoded AX.25 output group. Required.
.TP
.B "\-S destination, \-\-status\-in destination"
Listen for status that advertises a PCM destination instead of specifying PCM
groups explicitly. Explicit PCM inputs take precedence.
.TP
.B "\-A interface, \-\-iface interface"
Set default multicast interface.
.TP
.B "\-N name, \-\-name name"
Set service name advertised through Avahi. Default invocation name.
.TP
.B "\-T hops, \-\-ttl hops"
Set output multicast TTL. Default 10.
.TP
.B "\-p value, \-\-tos value, \-\-iptos value, \-\-ip\-tos value"
Set IP type-of-service value as a decimal integer. Default zero.
.TP
.B "\-v, \-\-verbose"
Increase diagnostics.
.TP
.B "\-V"
Print version and exit.
.SH INPUT AND OUTPUT
Configure radiod for flat, unsquelched PCM appropriate to packet audio; avoid
lossy compression and voice de-emphasis. Decoded output uses the ka9q-radio
AX.25 RTP payload convention and is advertised as _ax25._udp. It is not a PCM
audio stream. Packet and diagnostic text may also be written to standard
output.
.SH EXAMPLES
Decode an audio group and publish AX.25 packets:
.PP
.nf
packetd \-I packet\-pcm.local \-R ax25.local
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
radiod(8), aprsfeed(8), aprs(1), pcmrecord(1)
.PP
Project documentation: https://github.com/ka9q/ka9q-radio
